OL,3,GNEWSAChildren with a parent on benefits
OL,4,Ano longer eligible for priority
OL,5,Apre-school place
OL,6,
OL,7,FMost children with a parent on benefits
OL,8,Fwill not be eligible for priority
OL,9,Fnursery places from next year under
OL,10,Fchanges to the rules announced by
OL,11,FEducation Minister Paul Givan.
OL,13,FThe minister said he believed the rules
OL,14,F- known as Socially Disadvantaged
OL,15,FCircumstances (SDC) criterion - were
OL,16,Fnot "lawful" and were "discriminating
OL,17,Fagainst hard-working families".
OL,19,FHe added that the move would "level the
OL,20,Fplaying field" for pre-school
OL,21,Fadmissions.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
